{{971.primary_text}}

═══ HOW TO JUDGE ═══
1. Every claim marked contradicted or unsupported in round 1 must now be absent from the corrected article, or match the evidence exactly (same figure and scope, same title, same date). Quote the evidence.
2. Scan the WHOLE corrected article (all fields above) for every number, percentage, money amount, date, direct quote and person's title. Each must be supported by EVIDENCE A, B or C (copy a literal quote, max 30 words) or by a round-1 CHECKS line marked supported. Model-written material (the article itself, any canonical facts list) is NOT evidence.
3. The main claim of the title must be supported.
4. Every URL in Sources HTML must appear character-for-character in EVIDENCE A, B or C or in the source URLs given by the editor. Every figure in Canonical facts must appear in the Body HTML.
5. Compare the corrected Body HTML with the ORIGINAL BODY HTML. Any statement, name, company, regulator, status or source credit that appears in the corrected version but not in the original is new; a new item that is not supported by the evidence is a failure (the repair desk may not add facts).
6. verdict = HOLD if any check in 1-5 fails. Otherwise PASS.

